\subsection{Small leaderboards}\label{app:small}
We also applied the protocol to leaderboard matrices with too few benchmarks for a closure target: HELM Lite (10 scenarios), HELM Capabilities (5) and a block of 25 models in both HELM Lite and the Open LLM Leaderboard with 16 benchmarks (names matched by a fixed rule that excludes ambiguous names; 25 models appear in both sources, 23 with LiveBench and 72 in at least two). They are descriptive case studies with $N<12$ (or 16 with 12 families): greedy A is at or below random at every $k$ but the bands overlap throughout (Figure~\ref{fig:small}), and we draw no $k^*$ or hypothesis verdict from them.

