\section{Reproducibility, use of language models and forbidden material}\label{app:repro}
\paragraph{Code and data.}
The supplementary archive holds all code (Python 3.11, CPU only, versions pinned), the derived dense score matrices, the tidy result tables behind every number, figure and table here, a list of the departures from the study plan, and a README with the download pins for each public source, the commands, seeds and run times (each main run takes about 2--22 CPU minutes on one core, the history sweeps up to about an hour). Raw leaderboard files are not included and are re-downloaded from the pinned sources.

\paragraph{Use of language models.}
The research, the code and this text were produced by language-model agents working from a task specification; no person ran experiments or wrote text.

\paragraph{Excluded material.}
The task excluded one published study of this question and work citing it; none was read, searched for or used.
